Subject: [PATCH] Map larch theme block regions to manzanita

upgrade_d7_block's block_region map covers bartik->olivero and
doug_fir->madrone but not larch->manzanita, so every enabled larch
block placement (site footer 'LARCH bottom', sidebar emergency blocks,
etc.) fell through to the content region default and rendered directly
under the page title on every page. Larch region names map almost 1:1
onto manzanita; post_content goes to page_bottom.
---
--- a/modules/osu_migrate_content/migrations/upgrade_d7_block.yml	2026-07-02 09:14:03
+++ b/modules/osu_migrate_content/migrations/upgrade_d7_block.yml	2026-07-02 09:14:11
@@ -96,6 +96,22 @@
           sidebar_second: sidebar
           pre_footer: pre_footer
           footer: footer
+      larch:
+        # OSU Larch --> Manzanita
+        manzanita:
+          navigation: primary_menu
+          header: header
+          highlighted: highlighted
+          help: help
+          pre_content: full_top
+          content: content
+          post_content: page_bottom
+          sidebar_first: sidebar
+          sidebar_second: sidebar
+          pre_footer: pre_footer
+          footer: footer
+          page_top: page_top
+          page_bottom: page_bottom
     # If mapping fails, put the block in the content region.
     default_value: content
   weight: weight
